    description: "Swift: local functions with the same name in different enclosing initializers tie; their scope is the type, not the enclosing callable.\n\nREPRO: TCA Sources/ComposableArchitecture/Internal/Deprecations.swift, IfLetStore.open at L978 and L1012 (local functions in two different init bodies) share stable-id hash inputs and are split only by occurrence order, so editing one initializer can move the other's id. Found while counting WI-bubak: /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr3/bubak/RESULTS.md. Not checked in other languages with local functions (Kotlin, C#, Rust)."  # 17c1
